  <h3>Championship Machines &amp; Technical Highlights</h3>

  <h4>Pipeline &middot; 3lb Beetleweight Bar Spinner</h4>
  <p>
    <strong>November NHRL Pro Tour 3lb Champion (Undefeated 6&ndash;0) &middot; Reigning Midwest Robot Combat Association Champion (2024 &amp; 2025 Finals Winner).</strong> 
    Pipeline utilizes a massive AR500 steel spinning bar storing upwards of 800 Joules of kinetic energy, engineered to transfer peak impulse into opposing robots and accelerate them into arena ceilings.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Optimized Mass Budgeting:</strong> The internal chassis is heavily pocketed and additive-manufactured from high-impact engineering polymers, shifting maximum mass allowance into the exterior grade-5 titanium armor package and kinetic bar.</li>
    <li><strong>Centrifugal Duct Cooling:</strong> Internal chassis geometry utilizes the spinning weapon rotor as an air pump, pulling cooling drafts directly across brushless drive and weapon ESC heatspreaders to prevent thermal saturation during three-minute high-rate bouts.</li>
    <li><strong>Modular Front Geometry:</strong> Configurable between a low-slung bent-titanium wedge (countering horizontal cutters) and acute lifting forks (lifting opponents to achieve ideal hit geometry).</li>
  </ul>

